fixture hazard_loop_stick_held_pit
doc (movement review 4, M1) Review 4 (round 3's M3 is not closed): walking right off the chasm's edge into the spikes, holding right throughout, as hazard_respawn_stays_off_the_lip does. The 16 u margin puts the respawn at x 453 u, 27 u from the edge, and the stick still held walks Ash back off it 7 ticks later, inside the 20 f of hazard invulnerability, well inside a human's reaction time (about 12 ticks): the respawn-and-fall loop still runs, every 29 to 30 frames instead of every 23.
room test/spike_chasm
spawn 300 384
frames 200
input
  0..199 R
end
expect
  mark die1 0..199 event.hazard=1
  at die1 ground=1 x<=454u
  # What the margin was meant to buy: no second death while the stick is still held from the first.
  never die1+1..die1+60 event.hazard=1
end
